This example defines a function template 'findMax' that compares two values of any comparable type. The template parameter 'T' allows the function to work with both integers and doubles without rewriting the function. In 'main', 'findMax' is called with different data types, demonstrating how templates enable generic programming in C++, promoting code reuse and type safety.

