#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    sigjmp_buf env;
    int val = sigsetjmp(env, 1);  // Saves the context and signal mask
    if (val == 0) {
        printf("Executing initial code\n");
        siglongjmp(env, 1);  // Jumps back, restoring the signal mask
    } else {
        printf("Returned from siglongjmp with signal mask restored\n");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

This example shows sigsetjmp saving the execution context and the signal mask because the savemask argument is set to 1. When siglongjmp is called, it restores both the context and the saved signal mask, causing the program to jump back to the point after sigsetjmp. The output demonstrates the jump and restoration, highlighting how the signal mask is handled to maintain signal state consistency.

