This example demonstrates the use of std::streamsize as the type for the variable 'size', which specifies the number of characters to read from standard input. The read() function uses this type to determine how many characters to transfer. This showcases how std::streamsize is integral to managing I/O buffer sizes and character counts in a type-safe, portable manner within C++ streams.

